  <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__items">
        <div class="field__item"><p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">Broward County has 31 cities and each has a governing body with members elected by their voters. Each city has a Charter which stipulates the term of the office and the frequency of the elections.</p><p>March Election Options – If your city has elections in March, you have the option to vote-by-mail or in-person at your assigned polling place on Election Day.&nbsp; <a href="/voters/vote-mail-information" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="24fc2f0c-9a37-4e10-aa26-b08b6a43641e" data-entity-substitution="canonical" title="Vote By Mail">Click Here</a> to request Vote-by-Mail ballot</p><p>Candidate Qualifying - Candidates running for Municipal office will qualify with the City Clerk. All campaign documents are filed with and fees are paid to the City Clerk. Aspiring candidates should check with their City Clerk for qualifying dates and other pertinent information.</p><p><strong>*MUNICIPAL ELECTION DATE: </strong><em><strong>November 3, 2026 General Elections</strong></em><br><strong>Voter Registration Deadline</strong> – Monday, October 5, 2026<br><strong>Deadline to request that a VBM ballot be mailed to you –&nbsp;</strong><br>5:00 p.m. on Thursday, October 22, 2026</p><p><strong>*MUNICIPAL ELECTION DATE: </strong><em><strong>March 9, 2027 Municipal Elections</strong></em><br><strong>Voter Registration Deadline</strong> – Monday, February 8, 2027<br><strong>Deadline to request that a VBM ballot be mailed to you –&nbsp;</strong><br>5:00 p.m. on Thursday, February 25, 2027</p><style>td {
    border-color: inherit;
    border-style: solid;
    border-width: 1px;
    padding: 10px;
}</style></div>
  </div>
